rebuttal.value:
We thank all reviewers for their valuable feedback and suggestions. We'll address each reviewer's questions below individually.

Taking the reviewers’ suggestions into consideration, we have:
- Added several example jupyter notebooks to the open-source repository, including:
    - Minimal example of benchmarking a model using _folktexts_ tasks - [link](https://socialfoundations.github.io/folktexts/notebooks/minimal-example.html);
    - Example of using _folktexts_ with a different dataset - [link](https://socialfoundations.github.io/folktexts/notebooks/custom-dataset-example.html);
    - Example of defining a custom prediction task with _folktexts_ - [link](https://socialfoundations.github.io/folktexts/notebooks/custom-acs-task-example.html);
- Extended related work, including discussion of [Slack et al. (2023)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2304.13188), [Hegselmann et al. (2023)](https://proceedings.mlr.press/v206/hegselmann23a/hegselmann23a.pdf), [Tamkin et al. (2023)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2312.03689), and [Liu et al. (2024)](https://aclanthology.org/2024.naacl-long.198.pdf).
- Added results for all four additional ACS-based tasks to the appendix (ACSEmployment, ACSMobility, ACSTravelTime, and ACSPublicCoverage);
	- Results for the commute time prediction task (ACSTravelTime) are shown as an example in the 1-page rebuttal PDF.
- Added an appendix with extended analysis of calibration fairness among tested LLMs;
- Added confidence intervals to plots of calibration curves;
	- An example of sub-group calibration plot with confidence intervals is shown on the 1-page rebuttal PDF (the remaining plots will be available in the paper appendix).
- Standardized font-size among plots to a more readable (larger) size;
- Applied a continuous color map to the worst and best metric values in each column of Table 1 (for easier readability);
- Corrected typos and minor incoherences pointed out by reviewers;
	- Including an updated Figure 5 (shown in the rebuttal PDF).
- Improved general package documentation and created a live website with code documentation and example jupyter notebooks - [link](https://socialfoundations.github.io/folktexts/index.html);

---

We believe the updated paper and repository represent a definitive improvement over the previously submitted version. We hope these changes have addressed any remaining concerns regarding our contributions. Please let us know of any further questions you may have.

